.Rhistory
.RData
*.parquet
*.rds

# Bulk data stays out of git. Written as `data/*` rather than `data/` so the
# negation below can take effect: git does not descend into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so `data/` + `!data/x` silently keeps ignoring x.
data/*
# ...but world_records.csv is hand-maintained REFERENCE data, not bulk data.
# It is small, reviewable, and every "% of world record" on the site is wrong
# without it — so it belongs in git.
!data/world_records.csv
# Same class: the forward athletics calendar is hand-maintained and CANNOT be
# regenerated. competition_catalogue.parquet is built from harvested history, so
# it structurally cannot hold a meet that has not happened yet — which is the
# whole reason this file exists. Losing it means retyping every meet.
!data/athletics_calendar.csv
# Same class again: the Diamond League discipline grid and qualifying counts are
# transcribed by hand from a World Athletics regulation PDF and a season grid.
# Not derivable from anything we harvest, and re-transcribing 32 rows from a PDF
# is exactly the error-prone step this file exists to avoid repeating.
!data/diamond_league_2026.csv
# Documentation, not data -- names the canonical tables so `data/`'s ~1,500
# gitignored entries don't leave every clone guessing what's real. Small,
# reviewable, and exactly the file a repo-cleanup pass exists to write.
!data/README.md

# Blog export staging dir — build artefacts, republished on every run
blog/

# Archived data awaiting its 90-day retention window. Currently 17 GB, and it
# had NO ignore rule until 2026-09-04 — so any `git add -A` in this repo would
# have tried to commit all of it. The contents are already-superseded copies of
# gitignored `data/` files; nothing here is reviewable source.
_archive/

# Run logs from backtests and harvests. Machine-generated, regenerated on every
# run, and no log file has ever been tracked here — written down so that stays
# a decision rather than an accident.
*_log.txt
